# Handholding for platform / setup steps

Ignasi prefers clear, click-by-click guidance when a task touches **external platforms** or multiple tools (Supabase, GitHub, Google AI Studio, terminal, browser, phone, etc.).

## When this applies

Any time instructions involve:
- A web dashboard (Supabase, GitHub, Google AI Studio, etc.)
- CLI tools (`npx`, `supabase`, `gh`, deploy)
- Env vars, API keys, secrets
- Copying values between places
- “One-time setup” before a feature works

## How to write instructions

- **Name the product and where to click** — e.g. “Supabase dashboard → left sidebar → SQL Editor → New query”
- **One step = one action** — don’t combine “create key and deploy function” in one bullet
- **Say what screen looks like / what to copy** — field names, example shapes (`https://xxxx.supabase.co`, `AIza…`)
- **Say where the value goes next** — “paste into Terminal” / “save in `.env.local` as `VITE_…`”
- **Warn what NOT to use** — e.g. service_role vs anon; never commit secrets
- **Success check** — how to know the step worked (green Run, “Deployed”, no error in app)
- **If UI moved** — note menus change; offer alternate paths or what to search for
- Prefer a short **overview** (why / order), then the detailed steps

## Tone

Assume less familiarity with dashboards and CLI. Be patient and specific; avoid “just configure Supabase” without the clicks.
